      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pedro Sancho",
          "subtitle": "Card game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Pedro variant (also called Nine-Five) for four to seven players. Six cards each; one round of bidding (0–18). High bidder names trumps; the 5 (pedro) and 9 (sancho) of that suit score 5 and 9 points. First to 100 wins. Bidder must lead trump; follow suit when trump is led."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Pedro variant from the USA; a trick-taking game with 5 and 9 as permanent trumps."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Four to seven; four may play as two partnerships (partners opposite)."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard 52-card deck."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard 52-card deck."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Six cards each (most sources); some deal as far as cards go evenly. One round of bidding; dealer may take the bid by equalling the highest. High bidder declares trump."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
